# Design Language

Reference points: Apple, Linear, Notion, Stripe. Restrained, typographic, spacious.

## Principles

- **Whitespace carries hierarchy.** Reach for spacing before borders, fills, or dividers.
- **Typography does the work.** `tracking-tight` on large text, muted secondary text, at most two
  weights per screen. Prefer `text-balance` on headings and `text-pretty` on body copy.
- **Motion is subtle.** 150–250ms, translations of 8px or less, ease-out. Never bounce or spin
  decoratively. `prefers-reduced-motion` is honoured globally in `globals.css`.
- **Neutral-forward palette.** Near-black primary. `--brand` is reserved for identity moments and
  is deliberately low-chroma; it must never fill a large surface.
- **One primary action per view.** Everything else is a ghost button or a text link.

## Never

- Gradient backgrounds, gradient text, or coloured blur blobs
- Eyebrow "pill" badges above headings
- Oversized illustrations, 3D renders, or stock hero imagery
- Marketing sections — feature grids, testimonials, logo walls, pricing tables — unless asked for
- Emoji as iconography; use `lucide-react` at `size-4`
- Heavy shadows. Elevation comes from a hairline border or a barely-there shadow

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ Startup template
<span className="bg-brand-subtle text-brand rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs">Yeni</span>
<h1 className="bg-gradient-to-r from-indigo-500 to-pink-500 bg-clip-text text-5xl text-transparent">
<div className="flex gap-3">
  <Button size="lg">Başla</Button>
  <Button size="lg" variant="outline">Giriş</Button>
</div>

// ✅ Restrained
<h1 className="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">
<p className="text-muted-foreground text-lg text-pretty">
<div className="flex items-center gap-6">
  <Button>Başla</Button>
  <Link className="text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground text-sm transition-colors">Giriş</Link>
</div>
```
